/-!
# The natural restrictions following Definition C.1.22

For an exceptional A₇ block the central-cover cohomology bound proves
C_U(L)=1 and |U|=16. The original quotient embeds in SL₄(F₂), with U
identified equivariantly with its restricted natural module.

For an exceptional triple-cover A₆ block, the central cubic operator gives
an actual field of four elements acting on U. The original quotient embeds
in SL₃(F₄), with field-linear intertwining coordinates. The center-order-three
convention is the one in A.3.5; no sixfold universal cover is used.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.129; A.3.5, p.43; and I.1.5–6, p.408.
The definitions and public predicates in `BlockTypes.Basic` are unchanged.
-/
